note Exercism-style exercise "armstrong-numbers": https://exercism.org/tracks/python/exercises/armstrong-numbers
note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
note Return true when n equals the sum of its digits, each raised to the number of digits.
note Check it with: sh exercise.sh exercises/armstrong-numbers
om2
fn armstrong n ulong to bool
k = ulong 0
v = n
while true bound 20
k = add k 1
v = div v 10
if eq v 0
break
end
end
s = ulong 0
v = n
for i ulong k
d = rem v 10
p = ulong 1
for j ulong k
p = mul p d
end
s = add s p
v = div v 10
end
ret eq s n
end
